DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20210118
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Birthday of Martin Luther King\, Jr.
UID:c1bff0f4-425e-4d56-b830-6a5a874471d3
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Notes:\nThis holiday is designated as "Inauguration Day" in se
 ction 6103(c) of title 5 of the United States Code\, which is the law tha
 t specifies holidays for Federal employees. Federal employees in the Wash
 ington\, DC\, area are entitled to a holiday on the day a President is in
 augurated on January 20th for each fourth year after 1965.\n\nOPM.gov URL
 : https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/pay-leave/federal-holidays/ta
 bs/2021/
DTSTAMP:20261004T020006Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20210120
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Inauguration Day
UID:e12da69f-3bff-41b5-b04d-83c95acebe40
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Notes:\nThis holiday is designated as "Washington’s Birthday" 
 in section 6103(a) of title 5 of the United States Code\, which is the la
 w that specifies holidays for Federal employees. Though other institution
 s such as state and local governments and private businesses may use othe
 r names\, it is our policy to always refer to holidays by the names desig
 nated in the law.\n\nOPM.gov URL: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversig
 ht/pay-leave/federal-holidays/tabs/2021/
DTSTAMP:20261004T020006Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20210215
SEQUENCE:0
